A||N||3||Patrik||Cannot read error codes||||13
Z||000000||Patrik||09-12-1999||04:31 PM||||I bougth a Fiero SE V6 from 1985 a two months ago. When I was going to replace a bulb in the dashbord I discovered the there was no bulb in the "Check engine" light. Hmm... maybe that's why the car was so cheap... I replaced the bulb and naturally "Check engine" lights up when the ignition is turned on, and it stays on. I have tried to read the error codes by shorting the diagnostic connector to ground but the "Check engine" light does not flash any codes. The only thing that happens is that there is a buzzing sound from the throttle body in the engine (or somewhere around there).<P>My connector looks like this:<P>Passenger side	OOOOOX	     Driver side<BR>		XXOOXX<BR>		^^<BR>(X=Pin   O=No pin)<P>I have shorted the two pins marked by "^" (the two pins in the lower row, closest to the passenger side). The second pin from the left has +5V when the ignition is on.<BR>These are the pins indicated by my Haynes service manual.<P>The car runs fine except for rough idle sometimes and a bit of hesitation when it's cold.<BR>Could someone please help me with this so that I can find out what's wrong.<P>Regards, <BR>Patrik||||reg||13
Z||000001||Gokart||09-12-1999||06:08 PM||||I'm sure somebody will post after me and tell you what that means or what you may have done wrong, but in the meantime get yourself a GM scanner at the auto parts store. This way theres no mistakes or guess work and they are inexpensive.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-12-1999||07:57 PM||||I have an 85 v6 as well, and from your description those are the right pins to jump.<BR>if you short it out go to where the air filter hose meets the intake manifold.  You shoudl see there the TPS and below it the IAC.  If the IAC makes noise continually, then it should be in diagnostic mode.  You say it doesnt show any codes?<BR>does the check engine light do anything? (at least the 1-2) code?<BR>if not i think it might be best to borrow a code reader and see what it says.  if the check engine light is ALWAYS on, i would guess there is a wacky wire somewhere relating to the light.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||petealft||09-14-1999||07:37 AM||||hey pat, I just bought an 85 2m6 with a similar problem only the light never comes on .  I reacently posed this problem on this site. I got a bunch of sugestions on how to rectify the problem. ya see, my car will start and die in the same breath.  nothing worked and i lost the posted question.  so good luck ,and keep your eye on this sight. ya might loose it before the problem is solved.(like me.)||||reg||8
